            "text": ", giving a nuttier flavour and a slightly denser crumb. Honey replaces caster sugar for a gentle sweetness without heaviness. Spelt absorbs liquid faster than plain flour, so the dough will feel soft and sticky; adding extra flour will make the scones dry and tough."
          }
        ]
